# Leave NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL empty for web (uses relative URLs)
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=

# Multiplayer server (Cloudflare Worker in party/). Leave unset for local dev
# (uses localhost:8787 with `cd party && npm run dev`).
# Production builds without it hide multiplayer.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MULTIPLAYER_HOST=edy-on-bike-multiplayer.<subdomain>.workers.dev

# Upstash Redis (leaderboard, run tickets and rate limiting). Without it, local dev uses
# data/leaderboard.json and in-memory limits. The first complete pair wins
# (see REDIS_ENV_CANDIDATES in lib/leaderboard.ts):
#   storage_KV_REST_API_URL / storage_KV_REST_API_TOKEN   (current Vercel Marketplace connection)
#   KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN
#
# Where each pair comes from:
#   - Vercel Marketplace (Storage tab -> Upstash) injects KV_REST_API_URL/KV_REST_API_TOKEN,
#     prefixed with the connection's "custom prefix" if one was set. The live project uses the
#     prefix "storage", hence storage_KV_*. Pull them locally with `vercel env pull .env.local`.
#   - The unprefixed KV_* pair is what a connection without a prefix injects (it may also be
#     left over from a deleted database, which is why storage_KV_* is checked first).
#   - UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL/TOKEN are the names shown in the Upstash console; use them when
#     pasting credentials by hand.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
